<p class="prose">A fixed number of samples, whatever the span. That is <code>integral</code>'s rule — a fixed amount of work rather than a tolerance test — and it is what makes a drawing terminate and come out the same on every machine.</p>
<p class="prose">The span carries units, and so does what the function returns. Both axes are labelled from the dimensions rather than from anything the author writes twice.</p>
