<p class="prose">The shape <code>augment</code> builds, which is how a worksheet plots something it just computed: two columns joined into a table of points.</p>
<div class="step"><span class="name">t</span><span class="eq">=</span>range(0, 8)<span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]</span></div>
<div class="step note">fn drop defined</div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">fallen</span><span class="eq">=</span>augment(t s, map(drop, t))<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">augment([0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8] s, map(drop, [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]))</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">[[0 s, 0 m], [1 s, 2.45 m], [2 s, 9.8 m], [3 s, 22.05 m], [4 s, 39.2 m], [5 s, 61.25 m], [6 s, 88.2 m], [7 s, 120.05 m], [8 s, 156.8 m]]</span></div>
<div class="step">plot(fallen)</div>
